   "key": "§ Emuqu > Privacy",
   "hash": "c5b080fde6112b66",
   "does": "No server/accounts; iCloud sync off until enabled; table of third-party egress: CloudKit (encrypted, no HealthKit data), hosted AI (with consent; on every turn the live-state block from AssistantContext.renderLiveStateForCloud; DeepSeek PRC disclosure in ProviderConsentSheet), Apple Intelligence row: Quick sends nothing beyond web search/map lookups; with a consented Grok or DeepSeek, Auto sends classifier-flagged turns and Deep every turn to it (TierProviderMapper.autoMapping/deepMapping, reached only while Apple is the selected provider) with the same data a hosted turn carries; in every tier mode voice turns and email/directions/web-search requests go to the first consented hosted provider (TurnRouter voice bypass and action-intent override). Then Apple speech, Tavily/Anthropic web search, MET Norway at ~1 km (WeatherService rounds to 2 decimals), Overpass, Apple geocoder, OpenTopoData ~11 m, Hugging Face for the WhisperKit model. The closing paragraph says Quick/Auto/Deep apply only with Apple selected and that Auto and Deep can send a turn to a consented Grok or DeepSeek. API keys in Keychain ThisDeviceOnly, never synced (APIKeyStore). Overpass requests carry a User-Agent with the author's email (OverpassClient) — identifies the app to the operator, not data sent to the author. The iCloud row adds that sync is for the iCloud account it was turned on with and turns itself off on another account (CloudAccountGuard.stopSync).",
